Virtual Box:
If we want to perform on different OS, without disturbing host OS, we can use Virtual box and virtual box is a software.There are lot of virtual box available.Most commonly used are below two
1.Vmware player
2.Oracle Virtual box
 Using virtual box we can create multiple virtual machine on the same hardware(host machine hardware) same like our computer and on that we can create and install our linux OS or any other OS

CentOS vs CentOS Stream

Earlier all updates follow below way
Fedora -> RHEL -> CentOS
Now Its following below way
Fedora -> CentOS Stream ->RHEL (Here now updates come from CentOS to RHEL, here CentOS is upstream for updates to RHEL, so they called as CentOS Stream).
Both RHEL and CentOS is identical

Different ways to install OS.
1.Through CD drive - Just install the DVD which has OS and boot the system
2.Through ISO image - Just download the iso image of the OS and attach to virtual disc then access that virtual disc through console access.Every manufacture have console access, for dell its idrac.using that we can attach iso image to virtual disc and install OS to the system.
3.Through Network port - It will be useful when you want to install OS for 100's of computers. You access all machine IP and go to particular location through NFS or samba server and perform installation

