Virtual Machine Snapshot:
It allow to take snapshot of the current state of the machine.Sometime the machine may corrupt, by that time we can use that snapshot and restore the machine. Always take snapshot when the machine is powered off.

VM Management:
Most of the company manage the application using VM.like our qTest and my neoload controller and LG.If we want to increase the system resource, this can done by VM management.Every organization have their own VM management like Oracle virtual box, VM ware etc.Using that they will manage the VM. Like increase the system resources(CPU, RAM, Disk) etc

What is Actual Size and Virtual Size in VM:
Virtual Size: Amount of size we allocated during creation of VM eg 20GB
Actual Size: Only few percentage of size only allocated from Virtual size to VM. like out of 20 only 4 GB allocated to VM.But during runtime if we need more size, it will automatically get from host disk